     1,
     "<div>Hi Leanne,</div><div><br></div><div>This is a question for Ilya I think. I ran your code and got a nice plot of a volcano. But I can see the part of the runauto function that fails is the bit pasted below. One way you could try and check what&#39;s going on is by stepping through runauto line by line and see what&#39;s going wrong at the point below.</div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;font-size:13.3333px;outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\">if (hgt &lt; 0) {\r\n            soil0 &lt;- is_raster(tea) + tr\r\n            heatdown &lt;- soil0 - tout[, , i]\r\n            heatup &lt;- mean(soiltemps$D200cm) - tout[, , i]\r\n            xx &lt;- tout[, , i] + dfsoil$x1 * heatdown + dfsoil$x2 * \r\n                heatup\r\n            if (save.memory) \r\n                xx &lt;- round(xx * 1000, 0)\r\n            tout[, , i + 1] &lt;- xx\r\n        }\r\n        else {\r\n            xx &lt;- is_raster(tr) + is_raster(tea)\r\n            if (save.memory) \r\n                xx &lt;- round(xx * 1000, 0)\r\n            tout[, , i] &lt;- xx\r\n        }</span></span></span> <br></div><div><br></div><div>All the best,<br>Mike<br></div>"
    ],
